                <pb facs="1058" n="900" xml:id="pg900"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to
                        the Secretary of Foreign Relations</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 3, dated January 8,
                    1906, I failed to mention the name of Mr. Michel Kouri among those of American
                    citizens desirous of procuring licenses.</p>
                <p>I would thank you to call the attention of the honorable secretary of finance to
                    Mr. Kouri’s case.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
